# OWASP — frontend

When editing Svelte code (legacy projects: React/Vue equivalents), enforce from `code-review/data/owasp-checklist.json`:

- Treat all API/user content as untrusted before rendering
- No `{@html}` with untrusted content without sanitization (DOMPurify); legacy React: no `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`, legacy Vue: no `v-html`
- No secrets, tokens, or connection strings in frontend bundle
- Sensitive data only via HTTPS; use `window.fetch` with credentials policy
- No sensitive data in URL query strings or localStorage unless encrypted
- Disable autocomplete on login/password fields
- Client validation is UX only — server must re-validate

## When the UI shows sensitive data (also see `apply-security-patterns`)

- **Client-side masking and route guards are UX only** — the server masks and authorizes; never
  rely on hiding a value the API already returned in full
- Expect the API to send **masked** identifiers in lists and full values only on detail views;
  don't request or cache more PII than the current view needs
- Send the CSRF **custom header** (e.g. `X-Requested-With`) on every mutating request from the
  fetch/XHR client; keep all state changes on non-GET verbs
